IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tcpss-customer`

-- Telecommunications (Customer Service Guarantee) Standard 2023 (ACMA) -- the performance standards (ss 115), the scale of
-- damages (s 117) and the waiver rules (s 120) the Act leaves to the ACMA, read from the deposited instrument. A module beside
-- tcpss-customer.l4; it works out the two facts that module asks for ("my provider broke a customer service standard in my
-- case", "the amount the scale of damages sets") and passes them to its questions, restating none of the Act's rules.
--
-- SEAT: the phone customer, as in tcpss-customer.l4. "My phone line was connected late, or a fault was repaired late, or the
-- technician missed the appointment. What period did my provider have, did it break the guarantee, and how much must it pay me?"
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 1, compilation date 19 August 2026, includes amendments up to F2026L01056 (register id
-- F2026C00929), deposited at ../../../telecommunications-customer-service-guarantee-standard-2023/registers/source-bundle/
-- F2023L01140.txt (retrieved 2026-10-23).
--
-- UNITS. The Standard counts in business days (Acts Interpretation Act s 2B): the customer states how many business days after
-- the provider received the request or report the work was done, and how many business days it was late; the module never
-- turns a calendar date into business days. A request or report received after 5 pm counts as received the next business day
-- (s 6(2)); the customer counts from that day.
--
-- IN: ss 6 (CSG service, specified service), 10(1), (4), 11, 12, 14, 15, 17, 19(2)-(5), 20, 21, 22, 23 (as a fact), 24-27 (as
-- facts, with the notice deadlines), 32 and Schedule 1 (connection periods), Schedule 2 (contraventions and damages), 34
-- (waivers, with the written statement and the effective day). The provider's duties are also written as regulative rules.
-- OUT: s 8 record keeping, s 9 information duties, s 16, ss 28-31 (publication and the ACMA's temporary exemptions, asked
-- only as "the provider holds a temporary exemption"), s 35, Part 6 beyond s 39 (contraventions first occurring before 31 August 2023
-- are under the 2011 Standard, which is not deposited; the date question says so), Schedule 3 (extreme weather criteria, a fact).

§ `Telecommunications (Customer Service Guarantee) Standard 2023 -- the customer's questions`

§§ `ss 11, 12, Schedule 1 -- my connection period`

-- s 11(1): the Schedule 1 period applies if "(a) the site ... is in close proximity to an external plant facility used to
-- supply the service; and (b) the facility has sufficient capacity available"; (2): otherwise "a period within 20 business
-- days from the date of the customer's request". Schedule 1 item 201: an in-place connection, "2 business days after the
-- carriage service provider receives the request"; item 202: (a) an urban centre of 10 000 or more, 5 business days; (b) an
-- urban centre or other recognised community grouping of more than 2 500 but less than 10 000, 10; (c) more than 200 but not
-- more than 2 500, 15; (d) anywhere else, 15.
DECLARE `Where my site is` IS ONE OF
    `an urban centre of 10 000 people or more`
    `an urban centre or community of more than 2 500 but fewer than 10 000 people`
    `an urban centre, locality or community of more than 200 but no more than 2 500 people`
    `a locality or community of more than 200 people, outside an urban centre`
    `somewhere else (200 people or fewer, or no recognised community)`

GIVEN `the site` IS A `Where my site is`
      `it has an in-place connection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is close to a facility with capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the guaranteed maximum connection period` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is close to a facility with capacity`)
    THEN 20
    ELSE IF `it has an in-place connection`
         THEN 2
         ELSE CONSIDER `the site`
              WHEN `an urban centre of 10 000 people or more` THEN 5
              WHEN `an urban centre or community of more than 2 500 but fewer than 10 000 people` THEN 10
              OTHERWISE 15

@export How many business days does my provider have to connect my phone service under the customer service guarantee (s 11, Schedule 1)?
GIVEN `the site` IS A `Where my site is` @desc Where the site is, by the Australian Bureau of Statistics' urban centres and localities: an urban centre of 10 000 or more, a centre or community of 2 501 to 9 999, of 201 to 2 500, a locality of more than 200 outside an urban centre, or elsewhere
      `it has an in-place connection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the site has an in-place connection: a previous working service there was cancelled and can be reconnected or reactivated automatically
      `it is close to a facility with capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the site is in close proximity to an external plant facility used to supply the service, and that facility had enough capacity when you asked
GIVETH A NUMBER
`My guaranteed connection period in business days` MEANS
    `the guaranteed maximum connection period` `the site` `it has an in-place connection` `it is close to a facility with capacity`

§§ `ss 14, 15, 17 -- my repair period`

-- s 14(2): an urban centre of 10 000 or more: "the end of the first full business day after the carriage service provider
-- receives the report"; (3): an urban centre under 10 000 or a locality or community of more than 200: "the end of 2 full
-- business days after"; (4): elsewhere, 3. s 15: at a (3) or (4) site, 1 full business day if the fault "can be rectified
-- without: (i) external or internal plant work; or (ii) the carriage service provider attending the premises", or the
-- service was disconnected by an administrative error that does not involve damage to a facility.
GIVEN `the site` IS A `Where my site is`
      `it can be fixed remotely, or was an administrative disconnection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the guaranteed maximum rectification period` MEANS
    IF `the site` EQUALS `an urban centre of 10 000 people or more`
    THEN 1
    ELSE IF `it can be fixed remotely, or was an administrative disconnection`
         THEN 1
         ELSE IF `the site` EQUALS `somewhere else (200 people or fewer, or no recognised community)`
              THEN 3
              ELSE 2

@export How many full business days does my provider have to repair a fault in my phone service under the customer service guarantee (ss 14, 15)?
GIVEN `the site` IS A `Where my site is` @desc Where the site is, by the Australian Bureau of Statistics' urban centres and localities
      `it can be fixed remotely, or was an administrative disconnection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fault can be fixed without plant work and without a technician coming to your premises, or your service was cut off by the provider's administrative error with no damage to a facility
GIVETH A NUMBER
`My guaranteed repair period in full business days` MEANS
    `the guaranteed maximum rectification period` `the site` `it can be fixed remotely, or was an administrative disconnection`

§§ `ss 10, 21 to 27, Schedule 2 item 101(2) -- is my provider excused`

-- s 10(1): a standard "does not apply" where the customer refused a reasonable offer of an interim or alternative service,
-- or accepted an alternative service after a fully informed offer of both. Schedule 2 item 101(2): no delay is counted "if a
-- carriage service provider provides the customer with an interim service for the duration of the delay". s 21: exempt if
-- it supplies the customer "more than 5 eligible telephone services at one time". s 22: maintenance or upgrading, but where
-- the effect is no service at all, only with "reasonable notice". s 23: credit standing (as a fact). s 24: "circumstances
-- beyond the control" (damage it did not cause, a natural disaster or extreme weather causing mass outages, emergency
-- assistance to a public authority, no lawful access, a law); s 25(2): the exemption "is taken never to have applied" if the
-- provider does not give the s 26 statement (within 10 business days, or 14 weeks for no lawful access or a law) or the s 27
-- general notice (published within 9 business days). s 31: a temporary exemption granted by the ACMA.
DECLARE `What excuses my provider` IS ONE OF
    `nothing`
    `I refused its reasonable offer of an interim or alternative service, or accepted an alternative service it fully explained`
    `it supplied me an interim service for the whole delay`
    `it supplies me more than 5 eligible telephone services`
    `maintenance or upgrading, with reasonable notice to me where I was left without service`
    `my credit standing, or an unpaid-charge disconnection that complied with s 23`
    `circumstances beyond its control, and it gave me the s 26 statement or published the s 27 notice in time`
    `circumstances beyond its control, but it gave neither the s 26 statement nor the s 27 notice in time`
    `an ACMA temporary exemption covering my area`

GIVEN `the excuse` IS A `What excuses my provider`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my provider is excused` IF
        (NOT (`the excuse` EQUALS `nothing`))
    AND (NOT (`the excuse` EQUALS `circumstances beyond its control, but it gave neither the s 26 statement nor the s 27 notice in time`))

§§ `Schedule 2 -- the scale of damages`

-- Schedule 2 item 102: "residential/charity customer" means a residential customer or a charitable or welfare organisation;
-- item 103: every other customer is a "business customer".
DECLARE `Kind of customer` IS ONE OF
    `a residential customer, or a charitable or welfare organisation`
    `a business customer`

DECLARE `What went wrong` IS ONE OF
    -- item 201
    `my phone service was connected late`
    -- item 203
    `a fault in my phone service was repaired late`
    -- items 202, 204
    `call waiting, forwarding, barring, number display or display blocking was connected or repaired late`

-- Items 201 and 203: "for each business day of delay ... (a) in the first 5 business days of delay: (i) ... residential/charity
-- customer -- $14.52; and (ii) ... business customer -- $24.20; and (b) after the first 5 business days of delay -- $48.40".
-- Items 202 and 204 (an enhanced call handling feature): with 2 or more features not connected or rectified, the same; with
-- one, $7.26 and $12.10 for the first 5 days, then $24.20. Amounts are in cents to keep the arithmetic exact.
GIVEN `what` IS A `What went wrong`
      `customer` IS A `Kind of customer`
      `two or more features` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the cents a day in the first 5 business days` MEANS
    IF `what` EQUALS `call waiting, forwarding, barring, number display or display blocking was connected or repaired late` AND (NOT `two or more features`)
    THEN IF `customer` EQUALS `a business customer` THEN 1210 ELSE 726
    ELSE IF `customer` EQUALS `a business customer` THEN 2420 ELSE 1452

GIVEN `what` IS A `What went wrong`
      `two or more features` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the cents a day after 5 business days` MEANS
    IF `what` EQUALS `call waiting, forwarding, barring, number display or display blocking was connected or repaired late` AND (NOT `two or more features`)
    THEN 2420
    ELSE 4840

GIVEN `what` IS A `What went wrong`
      `customer` IS A `Kind of customer`
      `two or more features` IS A BOOLEAN
      `business days of delay` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the scale amount for the delay` MEANS
    ((`the cents a day in the first 5 business days` `what` `customer` `two or more features` TIMES `the first days`)
     PLUS (`the cents a day after 5 business days` `what` `two or more features` TIMES `the later days`)) DIVIDED BY 100
    WHERE
        `the first days` MEANS IF `business days of delay` GREATER THAN 5 THEN 5 ELSE `business days of delay`
        `the later days` MEANS IF `business days of delay` GREATER THAN 5 THEN `business days of delay` MINUS 5 ELSE 0

-- Schedule 2 item 101(1): a delay is "exceeding the guaranteed maximum connection period", "exceeding the guaranteed maximum
-- rectification period", or, where the provider and the customer arranged a particular day or period (ss 12, 17), "not
-- complying with those arrangements". The customer states the business days the arrangement allowed, or 0 for none.
GIVEN `the guaranteed period` IS A NUMBER
      `the period our arrangement allowed` IS A NUMBER
      `business days it took` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the business days of delay` MEANS
    IF `business days it took` GREATER THAN `the period allowed`
    THEN `business days it took` MINUS `the period allowed`
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `the period allowed` MEANS
            IF `the period our arrangement allowed` GREATER THAN 0 THEN `the period our arrangement allowed` ELSE `the guaranteed period`

§§ `Part 4, Schedule 2 -- did my provider break the guarantee, and what must it pay`

DECLARE `My guarantee claim` IS ONE OF
    `the provider was late by this many business days, and the scale sets this many dollars` HAS `days late` IS A NUMBER, `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `no contravention: the work was done within the period allowed`
    `no contravention: the provider is excused or exempt (ss 10, 21-24, 31, Schedule 2 item 101(2))`

GIVEN `the guaranteed period` IS A NUMBER
      `the period our arrangement allowed` IS A NUMBER
      `business days it took` IS A NUMBER
      `the excuse` IS A `What excuses my provider`
      `what` IS A `What went wrong`
      `customer` IS A `Kind of customer`
      `two or more features` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My guarantee claim`
`the guarantee claim` MEANS
    IF `my provider is excused` `the excuse`
    THEN `no contravention: the provider is excused or exempt (ss 10, 21-24, 31, Schedule 2 item 101(2))`
    ELSE IF `the delay` EQUALS 0
         THEN `no contravention: the work was done within the period allowed`
         ELSE `the provider was late by this many business days, and the scale sets this many dollars` `the delay` (`the scale amount for the delay` `what` `customer` `two or more features` `the delay`)
    WHERE
        `the delay` MEANS `the business days of delay` `the guaranteed period` `the period our arrangement allowed` `business days it took`

@export My phone service was connected or repaired late. Did my provider break the customer service guarantee, and what does the scale of damages set (Schedule 2)?
GIVEN `what` IS A `What went wrong` @desc What was late: connecting your phone service, repairing a fault in it, or connecting or repairing an enhanced call handling feature (call waiting, forwarding, barring, number display or display blocking)
      `customer` IS A `Kind of customer` @desc Whether you are a residential customer or a charitable or welfare organisation, or a business customer
      `two or more features` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an enhanced call handling feature: whether two or more features were not connected or not repaired (ignored otherwise)
      `the guaranteed period` IS A NUMBER @desc The guaranteed maximum period in business days (from the connection or repair period questions)
      `the period our arrangement allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc If you and the provider arranged connection or repair on or by a later day, the business days that arrangement allowed; 0 if there was no such arrangement
      `business days it took` IS A NUMBER @desc How many business days after the provider received your request or fault report (counting a request after 5 pm as received the next business day) it connected or repaired the service, or how many have passed if it has not yet
      `the excuse` IS A `What excuses my provider` @desc Whether anything excuses the provider: an interim or alternative service you refused or it gave you, more than 5 services, maintenance with notice, your credit standing, circumstances beyond its control with the notice given in time, an ACMA temporary exemption, or nothing
GIVETH A `My guarantee claim`
`Did my provider break the guarantee` MEANS
    `the guarantee claim` `the guaranteed period` `the period our arrangement allowed` `business days it took` `the excuse` `what` `customer` `two or more features`

-- Schedule 2 item 205: "Missing an appointment on a day that is not a day in relation to which damages calculated in
-- accordance with item 201, 202, 203 or 204 are payable": per missed appointment, $14.52 (residential/charity) or $24.20
-- (business). s 20: an appointment for a time is kept if the provider is there "not later than 15 minutes after"; for a
-- window up to 4 hours, not later than 15 minutes after its end; for a window over 4 and up to 5 hours, within it (45 minutes
-- after its end at a Schedule 1 item 202(c) or (d) site if it must travel a long distance). s 19(4): either party may change
-- the appointment with at least 24 hours' notice or by agreement.
DECLARE `The appointment` IS ONE OF
    `for a particular time`
    `for a window of up to 4 hours`
    `for a window of more than 4 and up to 5 hours`
    `for a window of more than 4 and up to 5 hours, at a small or remote site the technician had to travel far to reach`

GIVEN `the appointment` IS A `The appointment`
      `minutes late after the time or the window's end` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointment was kept` IF
    CONSIDER `the appointment`
    WHEN `for a particular time` THEN `minutes late after the time or the window's end` AT MOST 15
    WHEN `for a window of up to 4 hours` THEN `minutes late after the time or the window's end` AT MOST 15
    WHEN `for a window of more than 4 and up to 5 hours` THEN `minutes late after the time or the window's end` AT MOST 0
    WHEN `for a window of more than 4 and up to 5 hours, at a small or remote site the technician had to travel far to reach` THEN `minutes late after the time or the window's end` AT MOST 45

@export My provider's technician did not turn up on time for an appointment. What does the scale of damages set for it (ss 19, 20, Schedule 2 item 205)?
GIVEN `customer` IS A `Kind of customer` @desc Whether you are a residential customer or a charitable or welfare organisation, or a business customer
      `the appointment` IS A `The appointment` @desc What the appointment was for: a particular time, or a window of up to 4 hours, or of 4 to 5 hours (and whether at a small or remote site the technician had to travel far to reach)
      `minutes late after the time or the window's end` IS A NUMBER @desc How many minutes after the appointment time (or the end of the window) the technician arrived; 0 if on time or within the window; a large number if no one came
      `it was changed with 24 hours' notice or by agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the provider changed the appointment by giving you at least 24 hours' notice, or with your agreement
      `delay damages are payable for that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the same day is already a day of delay for which connection or repair damages are payable
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What does the scale set for my missed appointment` MEANS
    IF `it was changed with 24 hours' notice or by agreement` OR `delay damages are payable for that day` OR `the appointment was kept` `the appointment` `minutes late after the time or the window's end`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `customer` EQUALS `a business customer` THEN 24.20 ELSE 14.52

@export How much must my provider pay me in customer service guarantee damages for this delay, using the ACMA's scale (ss 116, 117, Schedule 2)?
GIVEN `what` IS A `What went wrong` @desc What was late: connecting your phone service, repairing a fault, or an enhanced call handling feature
      `customer` IS A `Kind of customer` @desc Whether you are a residential customer or charity, or a business customer
      `two or more features` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an enhanced call handling feature: whether two or more features were affected (ignored otherwise)
      `the guaranteed period` IS A NUMBER @desc The guaranteed maximum period in business days
      `the period our arrangement allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc The business days a later arrangement allowed; 0 if none
      `business days it took` IS A NUMBER @desc How many business days after your request or report it took
      `the excuse` IS A `What excuses my provider` @desc What, if anything, excuses the provider
      `what my provider already credited or paid me for the same event` IS A NUMBER @desc What your provider has already credited or paid you under another right or remedy for the same event; 0 if nothing
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`How much guarantee damages must my provider pay under the scale` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the guarantee claim` `the guaranteed period` `the period our arrangement allowed` `business days it took` `the excuse` `what` `customer` `two or more features`
    WHEN `the provider was late by this many business days, and the scale sets this many dollars` d amount THEN
        `How much guarantee damages must my provider pay` amount `what my provider already credited or paid me for the same event`
    OTHERWISE `answered` 0

@export Taking the Standard's periods and scale, is my provider liable to pay me customer service guarantee damages (s 116(1))?
GIVEN `my provider supplies or offers that kind of service at my location` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your provider supplies, or offers to supply, that kind of service at your location
      `I signed a waiver of the guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you validly waived the customer service guarantee for this service
      `my service is a universal service phone line` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the service is a standard telephone service supplied under the universal service obligation
      `what` IS A `What went wrong` @desc What was late: connecting your phone service, repairing a fault, or an enhanced call handling feature
      `the guaranteed period` IS A NUMBER @desc The guaranteed maximum period in business days
      `the period our arrangement allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc The business days a later arrangement allowed; 0 if none
      `business days it took` IS A NUMBER @desc How many business days after your request or report it took
      `the excuse` IS A `What excuses my provider` @desc What, if anything, excuses the provider
GIVETH AN `Am I owed damages under the guarantee`
`Am I owed guarantee damages under the Standard` MEANS
    `Am I owed damages under the customer service guarantee` `my provider supplies or offers that kind of service at my location` `it broke the standard` `I signed a waiver of the guarantee` `my service is a universal service phone line`
    WHERE
        -- the customer type and the number of features change only the amount, not whether there was a contravention
        `it broke the standard` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the guarantee claim` `the guaranteed period` `the period our arrangement allowed` `business days it took` `the excuse` `what` `a residential customer, or a charitable or welfare organisation` FALSE
            WHEN `the provider was late by this many business days, and the scale sets this many dollars` d amount THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 39 (Part 6): a contravention that "occurred, or first occurred, before the commencement of the new CSG Standard" and was
-- not paid for before then is worked out under the 2011 Standard, which is not deposited. The 2023 Standard commenced on 31
-- August 2023 (endnote 3).
DECLARE `Which Standard applies` IS ONE OF
    `the 2023 Standard, encoded here`
    `the 2011 Standard (s 39), which is not deposited: this module's periods and amounts do not apply`

@export Which customer service guarantee standard decides a contravention that began on a given day (s 39)?
GIVEN `the day it began` IS A DATE @desc The day the contravention occurred or first occurred (for example, the day after the period ran out)
GIVETH A `Which Standard applies`
`Which Standard decides my claim` MEANS
    IF `the day it began` LESS THAN (Date 31 8 2023)
    THEN `the 2011 Standard (s 39), which is not deposited: this module's periods and amounts do not apply`
    ELSE `the 2023 Standard, encoded here`

§§ `s 34 -- waiving the guarantee`

-- s 34(3): a written waiver needs the s 34(5) information "immediately before" consent, a prominent title containing "waiver",
-- a recorded and dated consent, and a statement that the customer understands the consequences. (4): an oral waiver needs the
-- information in (5)(d)-(f), being told of the written statement and of the right to withdraw, and a recorded consent. (7):
-- after an oral waiver the provider "must, within 3 business days after the customer consents ..., give to the customer a
-- written statement". (8): a written waiver takes effect "on the day on which the customer consents"; an oral one "5 business
-- days after the day on which the customer consents ..., unless, before the end of that period, the customer withdraws".
DECLARE `How I waived` IS ONE OF
    `in writing`
    `orally`

DECLARE `My waiver` IS ONE OF
    `it takes effect on the day I consented (s 34(8)(a))`
    `it takes effect 5 business days after I consented, unless I withdraw my consent before then; the provider must give me a written statement within 3 business days (s 34(7), (8)(b))`
    `it has no effect: I withdrew my consent within the 5 business days (s 34(8)(b))`
    `it is not a valid waiver: the provider did not do what s 34(3) or (4) requires`
    `I cannot waive the guarantee for a universal service phone line (s 120(7), s 33)`

@export I agreed to waive the customer service guarantee. Is the waiver valid, and when does it take effect (ss 33, 34)?
GIVEN `how` IS A `How I waived` @desc Whether you consented in writing or orally (for example on the phone)
      `the provider followed the required steps` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, immediately before you consented, the provider gave you the required information (the service, the date, its details, your protections, a summary of what you give up, that you need not agree) and recorded your consent (in writing: under a title containing "waiver", with your statement that you understand the consequences; orally: telling you of the written statement and your right to withdraw)
      `I withdrew within 5 business days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an oral waiver: whether you withdrew your consent within 5 business days after giving it
      `my service is a universal service phone line` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the service is a standard telephone service supplied under the universal service obligation
GIVETH A `My waiver`
`When does my waiver take effect` MEANS
    IF `my service is a universal service phone line`
    THEN `I cannot waive the guarantee for a universal service phone line (s 120(7), s 33)`
    ELSE IF (NOT `the provider followed the required steps`)
         THEN `it is not a valid waiver: the provider did not do what s 34(3) or (4) requires`
         ELSE IF `how` EQUALS `in writing`
              THEN `it takes effect on the day I consented (s 34(8)(a))`
              ELSE IF `I withdrew within 5 business days`
                   THEN `it has no effect: I withdrew my consent within the 5 business days (s 34(8)(b))`
                   ELSE `it takes effect 5 business days after I consented, unless I withdraw my consent before then; the provider must give me a written statement within 3 business days (s 34(7), (8)(b))`

§§ `The provider's duties under the Standard, as rules` -- deadlines in business days

DECLARE `CSG party` IS ONE OF
    `my provider`
    `I, the customer`

DECLARE `CSG act` IS ONE OF
    `connect the service`
    `rectify the fault`
    `attend the appointment`
    `give me a written statement of the oral waiver`
    `give me the s 26 statement about the exemption`

-- s 11(3): "A carriage service provider must comply with a request by a customer for connection in the guaranteed maximum
-- connection period"; Schedule 2 items 201, 202: damages for each business day of delay.
GIVEN `the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `CSG party` `CSG act`
`the connection duty` MEANS
    PARTY `my provider`
    MUST  `connect the service`
    WITHIN `the period`
    LEST  BREACH BY `my provider` BECAUSE "s 11(3): connection not made in the guaranteed maximum connection period; damages per business day of delay under Schedule 2 item 201 or 202"

-- s 14(5): the provider "must, in the relevant guaranteed maximum rectification period, rectify a fault or service difficulty
-- that is reported to" it.
GIVEN `the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `CSG party` `CSG act`
`the repair duty` MEANS
    PARTY `my provider`
    MUST  `rectify the fault`
    WITHIN `the period`
    LEST  BREACH BY `my provider` BECAUSE "s 14(5): fault not rectified in the guaranteed maximum rectification period; damages per business day of delay under Schedule 2 item 203 or 204"

-- s 19(5): "A carriage service provider must keep an appointment to which the carriage service provider is a party." Counted
-- here in minutes after the time or the window's end, with the s 20 allowance.
GIVEN `the allowance in minutes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `CSG party` `CSG act`
`the appointment duty` MEANS
    PARTY `my provider`
    MUST  `attend the appointment`
    WITHIN `the allowance in minutes`
    LEST  BREACH BY `my provider` BECAUSE "s 19(5), s 20: the appointment was missed; damages under Schedule 2 item 205"

-- s 34(7): within 3 business days after an oral waiver, a written statement titled with the word "waiver".
GIVETH A DEONTIC `CSG party` `CSG act`
`the oral waiver statement duty` MEANS
    PARTY `my provider`
    MUST  `give me a written statement of the oral waiver`
    WITHIN 3
    LEST  BREACH BY `my provider` BECAUSE "s 34(7): no written statement of the oral waiver within 3 business days"

-- s 26(2)(b): a provider relying on s 24 must give each affected customer the statement "not later than 10 business days
-- after the first day on which the exemption becomes available"; if it does not (and does not use s 27), the exemption is
-- taken never to have applied (s 25(2)).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `CSG party` `CSG act`
`the exemption statement duty` MEANS
    PARTY `my provider`
    MUST  `give me the s 26 statement about the exemption`
    WITHIN 10
    LEST  BREACH BY `my provider` BECAUSE "s 26(2)(b), s 25(2): no statement within 10 business days, so the s 24 exemption is taken never to have applied"
